    "result_text": "The build is green. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `salutation` feature: the request may include a `title` (MR/MRS/MS/DR), and the owner's `salutation` is returned as `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\nI kept structural impact low by touching **4 files** and adding behaviour as small, self-contained units rather than growing any complex method:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` column field with its getter/setter, plus a tiny derived `getSalutation()` (the only new logic, CC 2). MapStruct auto-maps `title` in from the request and `salutation` out to the response by name, so **no mapper edit was needed** \u2014 avoiding an edit to the mapper interface entirely.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` to the `OwnerFields` input schema and a read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` response schema (drives DTO generation).\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title VARCHAR(10)` column (hsqldb is the test profile; per repo convention only this schema carries the evolving columns).\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended the trailing value for the new column to the 10 positional seed inserts.\n\nNo policy class or mapper changes were required \u2014 the derived getter + MapStruct auto-mapping keeps each changed function trivial. Full test suite: **BUILD SUCCESS** (1 run, 0 failures).",
